lorentz-factor.conceptual_definition:
The Lorentz factor, denoted by the Greek letter gamma (\
\gamma\
), is a fundamental quantity in special relativity that quantifies the extent to which relativistic effects, such as time dilation and length contraction, become significant for an object moving at a certain velocity. It is a dimensionless scalar that depends only on the relative speed between two inertial frames of reference.
